{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,pathlib\nobj={'sourceInformation':{'date':'2026-11-05 03:12:06','source':'Trauma Center: Second Opinion','plan':'PLAN.md','genre':'Surgical action / medical drama (Simulation)','perspective':'First-person fixed 3D operating field; cinematic character scenes','tech':'Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier, JavaScript ES modules, esbuild','artDirection':'Native low-poly 3D pixel art; original procedural tissue, instruments, portraits and hospital sets','animation':'Native HERO_CLIPS on custom hospital rigs; SpringChain, Squash and procedural anatomy / tool / face animation','audio':'Original code-synthesised chiptune music, instrument and monitor effects, formant-synthesised gibberish voices; music defaults to 10 percent','online':'AI Hub protocol v1 shared-world Consult for 1 to 4 players; local couch co-op','testing':'Headless simulation, complete bot campaign, browser input, audio synthesis, Hub harness and viewport checks; no physical controller or real iOS Safari available','research':'PLAN.md reports planner research into the source Wikipedia page, Hub protocol and engine spikes. Build research: engine GUIDE.md, ASSETS.md, API.md and Hub README.md.','environment':'Codex CLI (headless); Linux','model':'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort max','usage':'added on import'},'testingFeedback':['unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown'],'engineFeedback':['The native pixel renderer, declarative models, procedural audio and headless stepping work well together.','unknown','The deterministic surgical simulation, tool gestures, campaign and network codec.','unknown','none','A documented surgical-plane picking and HUD vector helper would reduce custom glue.'],'promptFeedback':['The original cast, operation beats and verified engine recipes made the design concrete.','The plan asks for a complete campaign while the task describes a vertical slice; I implemented the ten linked cases.','Keeping precision interaction readable on a TV while supporting mouse, keyboard, four pads and network seats.','Separate required mechanics from optional scene embellishments, and provide a compact acceptance checklist.'],'aiHub':{'name':'Trauma Ward: Critical Opinion','tagline':'The truth, stat.','description':'A rain-soaked surgical drama in Port Verity. Trace incisions, extract foreign bodies, face engineered pathogens and bring your patients home through ten operations or a shared Consult shift.','type':'Game','genre':'Simulation','source':'Trauma Center: Second Opinion','series':'Trauma Center','players':'1–4','controls':'Stick / WASD / mouse: aim; R2 / J / click: use; right stick / 1–8: tools; L2 / Space: gift; Options / Esc: pause.','tags':['3d','pixel art','story','co-op','boss fights','comedy']}}\npathlib.Path('../exit-interview.json').write_text(json.dumps(obj,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\npathlib.Path('src/content/about.js').write_text('export const INTERVIEW='+json.dumps(obj,indent=2)+';\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
