{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_127","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('../exit-interview.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text())\nd['sourceInformation'].update({\n 'tech':'JavaScript ES modules; unmodified Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (three.js r186, embedded Rapier); esbuild 0.28.2. Fully embedded single HTML.',\n 'artDirection':'Native low-poly 3D pixel art with original procedural anatomy, surgical instruments, hands, six character portraits and seven hospital sets; Kenney furniture props.',\n 'animation':'Native HERO_CLIPS on custom rigs, SpringChain and Squash; procedural tools, blinking, mouths, breathing, heartbeat, perfusion and ghost hands.',\n 'audio':'Original chiptune songs, instrument and monitor effects, and formant-synthesised gibberish voices, all generated in JavaScript. No audio assets; music defaults to 10%.',\n 'online':'AI Hub v1 shared-world Consult for 1-4 players, client 1.4.0; authoritative host/server, compact snapshots and remote interpolation. Standalone couch Consult for 1-4.',\n 'testing':'Full campaign to credits; tool/save rules; audio/analyser; mouse, keyboard and pad stubs; 14 viewports; 5 Hub scenarios. WebKit/Firefox fallback checked; real iOS Safari and physical pads unavailable.',\n 'research':'Planner reported source Wikipedia, Hub and engine spikes. Build research read PLAN.md, engine GUIDE/ASSETS/API, the engine release and official Hub protocol.',\n})\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n '15 distinct issues caught and fixed, grouping repeated model warnings by their root cause; details are recorded in tests/ISSUES.md.',\n '4 runtime, progression or multiplayer blockers; one additional packaging blocker. All are fixed.',\n 'The complete engine-driven campaign playthrough verified every scene and operation through credits, saves and unlocks. Separate-pad browser play caught a control-routing defect.',\n 'The short boot replay checked engine setup but did not expose gesture, controller-routing or visual layout problems.',\n]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n 'The native 3D-to-pixel renderer, declarative models, animation clips, procedural audio and headless replay work together through one import.',\n 'I initially omitted cameraTarget and underestimated curved-surface picking and visibility semantics; engine checks and browser tests exposed those assumptions.',\n 'A deterministic, rewindable surgical simulation with eight tool gestures, a campaign, a reusable bot and an authoritative shared world.',\n 'Coordinating curved anatomy, precise mouse picking, the retained pixel HUD, and independent controller seats.',\n 'none; pixel-engine.js is byte-identical to the shipping archive. All game systems and assets were added on top.',\n 'Add public line and circle primitives to the HUD.',\n]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n 'The original cast, patient hooks and verified engine recipes gave the game a concrete identity and a useful starting point.',\n 'The boundary between a feature-complete demo and the proposed ten-operation campaign was unclear; I implemented all ten linked cases.',\n 'Keeping precise surgical gestures, multiple input devices, time rewind and shared-state play coherent while preserving the drama.',\n 'State the required campaign length in TASK.md as well as in the plan.',\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPath('src/content/about.js').write_text('export const INTERVIEW='+json.dumps(d,indent=2)+';\\\\n')\nissues=Path('tests/ISSUES.md')\nissues.write_text(issues.read_text()+'''\\\\n11. WebKit phone emulation reported a coarse pointer with zero maxTouchPoints. Touch detection now recognizes that combination and shows the required gate.\\\\n12. Unused hand groups received null visibility, which the renderer treated as visible. They now receive a strict boolean; the browser checks only joined seats render.\\\\n13. The surgical HUD had low contrast, a cropped dose label, and narrow-device clutter. Corrected texture color space, anchored the tool card, moved stage data into the top strip, and simplified gated views.\\\\n14. The OR table obscured portrait faces. Portraits now stand in front of the set geometry.\\\\n15. Pause/settings drew a second HUD underneath the menu. Removed that overlay so menu text and prompts remain clear.\\\\n\\\\nAll fifteen issues are resolved. The complete suite passed 183 checks; final wheel/drop regression checks additionally passed in their affected scopes.\\\\n''')\nPY\nnode tools/build.mjs\nnode tests/run.mjs content\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_127","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('../exit-interview.json');d=json.loads(p.read_text())\nd['sourceInformation'].update({\n 'tech':'JavaScript ES modules; unmodified Pixel Engine 0.46.0 (three.js r186, embedded Rapier); esbuild 0.28.2. Fully embedded single HTML.',\n 'artDirection':'Native low-poly 3D pixel art with original procedural anatomy, surgical instruments, hands, six character portraits and seven hospital sets; Kenney furniture props.',\n 'animation':'Native HERO_CLIPS on custom rigs, SpringChain and Squash; procedural tools, blinking, mouths, breathing, heartbeat, perfusion and ghost hands.',\n 'audio':'Original chiptune songs, instrument and monitor effects, and formant-synthesised gibberish voices, all generated in JavaScript. No audio assets; music defaults to 10%.',\n 'online':'AI Hub v1 shared-world Consult for 1-4 players, client 1.4.0; authoritative host/server, compact snapshots and remote interpolation. Standalone couch Consult for 1-4.',\n 'testing':'Full campaign to credits; tool/save rules; audio/analyser; mouse, keyboard and pad stubs; 14 viewports; 5 Hub scenarios. WebKit/Firefox fallback checked; real iOS Safari and physical pads unavailable.',\n 'research':'Planner reported source Wikipedia, Hub and engine spikes. Build research read PLAN.md, engine GUIDE/ASSETS/API, the engine release and official Hub protocol.',\n})\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n '15 distinct issues caught and fixed, grouping repeated model warnings by their root cause; details are recorded in tests/ISSUES.md.',\n '4 runtime, progression or multiplayer blockers; one additional packaging blocker. All are fixed.',\n 'The complete engine-driven campaign playthrough verified every scene and operation through credits, saves and unlocks. Separate-pad browser play caught a control-routing defect.',\n 'The short boot replay checked engine setup but did not expose gesture, controller-routing or visual layout problems.',\n]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n 'The native 3D-to-pixel renderer, declarative models, animation clips, procedural audio and headless replay work together through one import.',\n 'I initially omitted cameraTarget and underestimated curved-surface picking and visibility semantics; engine checks and browser tests exposed those assumptions.',\n 'A deterministic, rewindable surgical simulation with eight tool gestures, a campaign, a reusable bot and an authoritative shared world.',\n 'Coordinating curved anatomy, precise mouse picking, the retained pixel HUD, and independent controller seats.',\n 'none; pixel-engine.js is byte-identical to the shipping archive. All game systems and assets were added on top.',\n 'Add public line and circle primitives to the HUD.',\n]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n 'The original cast, patient hooks and verified engine recipes gave the game a concrete identity and a useful starting point.',\n 'The boundary between a feature-complete demo and the proposed ten-operation campaign was unclear; I implemented all ten linked cases.',\n 'Keeping precise surgical gestures, multiple input devices, time rewind and shared-state play coherent while preserving the drama.',\n 'State the required campaign length in TASK.md as well as in the plan.',\n]\np.write_text(json.dumps(d,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPath('src/content/about.js').write_text('export const INTERVIEW='+json.dumps(d,indent=2)+';\\\\n')\nissues=Path('tests/ISSUES.md')\nissues.write_text(issues.read_text()+'''\\\\n11. WebKit phone emulation reported a coarse pointer with zero maxTouchPoints. Touch detection now recognizes that combination and shows the required gate.\\\\n12. Unused hand groups received null visibility, which the renderer treated as visible. They now receive a strict boolean; the browser checks only joined seats render.\\\\n13. The surgical HUD had low contrast, a cropped dose label, and narrow-device clutter. Corrected texture color space, anchored the tool card, moved stage data into the top strip, and simplified gated views.\\\\n14. The OR table obscured portrait faces. Portraits now stand in front of the set geometry.\\\\n15. Pause/settings drew a second HUD underneath the menu. Removed that overlay so menu text and prompts remain clear.\\\\n\\\\nAll fifteen issues are resolved. The complete suite passed 183 checks; final wheel/drop regression checks additionally passed in their affected scopes.\\\\n''')\nPY\nnode tools/build.mjs\nnode tests/run.mjs content\"","aggregated_output":"Built Trauma-Ward-Critical-Opinion-Trauma-Center-Second-Opinion-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261105-031206.html (6.10 MB)\n46/46 checks passed; 0 failures.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
