{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_144","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"node --input-type=module <<'JS'\nimport {readFileSync,writeFileSync,existsSync,readdirSync} from 'node:fs';import {createHash} from 'node:crypto';import {STEM,TITLE} from './src/core/meta.js';\nconst file='../'+STEM+'.html',html=readFileSync(file);for(const f of ['dist/game.html','index.html'])if(\"'!html.equals(readFileSync(f)))throw Error('\"'HTML copies differ: '+f);\nconst interview=JSON.parse(readFileSync('../exit-interview.json','utf8'));if(Object.keys(interview).join(',')\"'!=='\"'sourceInformation,testingFeedback,engineFeedback,promptFeedback,aiHub')throw Error('Interview schema');if(interview.sourceInformation.usage\"'!=='\"'added on import')throw Error('Usage metadata');if(interview.aiHub.name\"'!==TITLE)throw Error('\"'Title mismatch');\nconst tests=new Map();for(const scope of ['all','sim','browser','content','visual']){const report=JSON.parse(readFileSync('tests/results/'+scope+'.json'));for(const test of report.tests)tests.set(test.name,test);}const failed=[...tests.values()].filter(t=>\"'!t.pass);if(failed.length)throw Error(JSON.stringify(failed));\nconst result={uniqueChecks:tests.size,passed:tests.size,fullSuite:183,scopeCounts:{simulation:95,content:46,engine:4,browser:21,hub:5,visual:16},htmlBytes:html.length,htmlSHA256:createHash('\"'sha256').update(html).digest('hex'),metadataComplete:true,engineUnmodified:true,screenshots:readdirSync('tests/results/screens').filter(f=>f.endsWith('.png')).length};writeFileSync('tests/results/final-validation.json',JSON.stringify(result,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nconst images=readdirSync('tests/results/screens').filter(f=>f.endsWith('.png')).sort();writeFileSync('tests/results/screens/index.html','<\"'!doctype html><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Critical Opinion / Visual Checks</title><style>body{margin:24px;background:#101d2c;color:#f3e7c7;font:16px monospace}main{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr));gap:20px}img{width:100%;height:220px;object-fit:contain;background:#162c35}a{color:#76d7c3}figure{margin:0}</style><h1>Critical Opinion / visual checks</h1><main>'\"'+images.map(f=>'<figure><a href=\\\"'+f+'\\\"><img loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"'+f+'\\\"><figcaption>'+f.slice(0,-4)+'</figcaption></a></figure>').join('')+'</main>');\nconst progress=\"'`# Progress'\"\\\\n\\\\nStatus: COMPLETE. No outstanding implementation work.\\\\n\\\\n## Deliverables\\\\n- Root HTML: \"'${STEM}.html'\"\\\\n- Root exit-interview.json: validated exact TASK.md schema; all required source and feedback fields filled.\\\\n- Development folder: \"'${STEM}/'\"\\\\n- The root HTML, dev index.html and dist/game.html are byte-identical, standalone, embedded builds (\"'${html.length} bytes).'\"\\\\n- Open the HTML in a WebGPU browser. Browsers without WebGPU show a readable renderer notice and simulation-driven demonstration.\\\\n\\\\n## Identity and scope\\\\n- Title: \"'${TITLE}. Selected with Python secrets.randbelow from 50 brainstormed titles; record in title-selection.json.'\"\\\\n- Original surgical action / medical drama based on PLAN.md and TASK.md. All ten campaign cases and the morning ending are playable; Pile-Up Consult supports 1-4 couch or Hub seats.\\\\n- Eight physical surgical tools, triage, bone rotation, transplant and perfusion, both gifts, Code Blue, massage, four active strains, ghost hands and two-doctor assistance.\\\\n- Original six-character story, seven hospital sets, procedural anatomy, custom hand/tool/portrait/figure models and native animation. All audio generated in code; music defaults to 10%.\\\\n- Controller/keyboard/mouse menus, input-aware prompts, PlayStation/Xbox glyphs, settings, saves, replay log, results, pause Dev Mode and 10-second attract reel. Touch-only gate shows exact required text and no touch controls.\\\\n- Source Information and all feedback are in the paged About/Credits UI and exit interview; licence texts embedded.\\\\n\\\\n## Engine and network\\\\n- Pixel Engine 0.46.0 is unchanged. Every build compares its SHA-256 with the shipping archive.\\\\n- Unmodified Hub v1 client 1.4.0 is the first script. Shared-world authority runs independently of rendering, including renderer-free server hosting.\\\\n- Inputs 15 Hz, snapshots 12 Hz, keyframes 1 Hz, reliable events up to 4 Hz; token bucket, compact codec, remote interpolation, immediate local aim, correct rewind clock and per-seat ghost trails.\\\\n- No network outside a Hub session. All test servers used OS-picked loopback ports and were stopped; browsers closed.\\\\n\\\\n## Verification\\\\n- Full suite: 183/183 passed, including an actual engine-driven playthrough of every scene and operation through credits with saves/unlocks.\\\\n- Final affected-scope checks added drop cancellation, mouse-wheel menus, mixed mouse-and-pad independence and complete credits text fitting.\\\\n- Final combined evidence: \"'${tests.size}/${tests.size} unique checks pass: 95 simulation, 46 content/audio/packaging, 4 native engine, 21 browser/input, 5 Hub, 16 visual/viewport. See tests/results/final-validation.json.'\"\\\\n- Official Hub passed 2, 3 and 4 players; 150ms latency, 50ms jitter, 5% loss; host-leave; server host.\\\\n- Inspected all ten arenas, all six cast members, all seven rooms, all eight instruments, resuscitation, UI/feedback pages and fourteen viewport captures. \"'${result.screenshots} PNGs plus a gallery in tests/results/screens/index.html.'\"\\\\n- A final screenshot browser initially crashed before boot under shared-machine memory pressure. Retried with a 960x540 startup viewport, then captured full 1920x1080 frames; 16/16 passed. No game/GPU errors remained.\\\\n- WebKit iPhone/iPad and Firefox fallbacks were checked. Real iOS Safari and physical controller behavior were unavailable; standard pad stubs, touch profiles and audio analysis were used.\\\\n- 16 grouped issues fixed; 5 runtime/progression/multiplayer blockers and 1 packaging blocker. Details: tests/ISSUES.md.\\\\n\\\\n## Reproduce\\\\n- In the development folder: node tools/build.mjs\\\\n- One test command: node tests/run.mjs\\\\n- Scope filters: sim, content, engine, browser, hub, visual\\\\n- Balance report: node tests/balance.mjs\\\\n- Extension guide: docs/AUTHORING.md\\\\n\\\\nFinal HTML SHA-256: \"'${result.htmlSHA256}'\"\\\\n\"'`;\nwriteFileSync('\"'../PROGRESS.md',progress);console.log(JSON.stringify(result));\nJS\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
